  <h1>Stay with the story.<br/><em>Understand the words.</em></h1>
  <p class="nl-lead">A browser extension idea for the moments when an unfamiliar word interrupts your reading. Select a word or a passage, explore its meaning nearby, and keep your place.</p>
  <div class="nl-actions"><a class="nl-button" href="mailto:contact@dilum.io?subject=Pontix">Ask about the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="nl-secondary" href="/2000nl/">Explore 2000nl ↗</a></div>
  <p class="nl-access">An early prototype is being explored. Pontix is not available as a finished public extension.</p>
 </header>
 <section class="nl-steps" aria-label="The Pontix idea">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">01 · Read</p><h2>Start where you are.</h2><p>The article, webpage or passage you chose is the starting point. The idea is to bring language support into your reading.</p></div>
  <div><p class="eyebrow">02 · Understand</p><h2>A little help alongside.</h2><p>The early sidebar prototype explores selected-text translation, with multiple translation services and saved preferences.</p></div>
  <div><p class="eyebrow">03 · Connect</p><h2>Keep useful discoveries.</h2><p>The direction is to connect words you encounter with dictionary lookup and vocabulary practice in 2000nl. This connection is still in development.</p></div>
 </section>
 <section class="af-status"><p class="eyebrow">One learning world, different ways in</p><h2>Words from reading.<br/>Practice in 2000nl.</h2><p>Pontix explores the reading side of the same idea behind <a href="/audiofilms/">AudioFilms</a>: meet language in context, get help understanding it, and return to useful words in <a href="/2000nl/">2000nl</a>.</p><p>It is one of our earliest experiments. The interface, integrations and public availability are still taking shape. We’ll share the work and decisions in the <a href="/blog/">journal</a>.</p></section>
